+The color $C$ of a rasterized pixel is the interpolated vertex color [S1]. For a vertex $V_i$ with position $P_i = (u_i, v_i, w_i)$, the color attribute is $C_i = (u_i, v_i, w_i)$ [S1]. The interpolated color $C_{pixel}$ at a pixel is:
 $$ C_{pixel} = \frac{\sum \alpha_i C_i}{\sum \alpha_i} $$
